  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Sec. 3121(a) and Rev. Rul. 74-44, S corporation shareholder-employees must receive reasonable compensation before taking distributions. The IRS may recharacterize distributions as wages, triggering FICA taxes under Sec. 3101 and 3111 plus penalties.
Wrong (A): S corporation income is not subject to double taxation; it passes through to shareholders and is taxed once at the individual level.
