  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 163(j)(7)(C), an electing farming business is exempt from the interest limitation but must use the alternative depreciation system (ADS) for any property with a recovery period of 10 years or more. This generally results in longer depreciation periods for farm buildings and equipment.
Wrong (A): There is no requirement to switch to the cash method; the election affects depreciation methods, not the overall accounting method used by the farming business.
Wrong (B): The 30% ATI limitation is the general rule under Section 163(j); electing out removes this limitation entirely rather than imposing a lower 15% cap.
